<title>FRANCE: Bouygues in 500 mln Ffr Turkmenistan deal.</title>
<headline>Bouygues in 500 mln Ffr Turkmenistan deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French group Bouygues said on Monday it had signed a contract with the Turkmenistan government for the construction of the Ashkabad congress and fine arts complex.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the construction project was worth some 500 million francs and would begin in the coming weeks and last about 27 months.</p>
<p>It includes an opera theatre seating 2,800 with a stage of 500 sq metres and a conference centre with a capacity of 300 as well as a separate function room with a capacity of 800 and other rooms and conference facilities.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
